372421001-5c972665-b4b8-469d-a203-01be373152e7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785639947630519001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c25809c4-56c5-4a09-b6b1-94c7f3d2e929","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e690-1a68-813d-4fc9"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nBug tickets carry no record of WHICH detection channel found them (canary, CI, review bot, human audit, user report), so escape-channel trends are unmeasurable. Retroactive classification was rejected (unreliable); capture must happen at creation with zero added user friction.\n\n## Approach\nAutomated filers set an environment variable (e.g. REBAR_DETECTED_BY=canary|ci|review-bot) that is read at the create seam every ingress converges on — src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:create_core (:73) — NOT in the CLI arg parser, so library (_lib_writes.create_ticket), MCP (_mcp_writes.create_ticket), and CLI filers all get the stamp; scales to client projects because the filer owns its own env. Human/agent sources may pass an OPTIONAL '--detected-by <source>' flag; absent both, the field is simply unset (never required, never prompted). Document the flag in agent guidance and the bug-creation contract (see canary-hardening sibling).\n\nValidation policy (deterministic, never blocks filing): the value is a free-form token, normalized by strip() + lowercase. Empty or whitespace-only after strip -> treated as unset (field absent from the event). Any non-empty normalized value is stamped verbatim — there is NO enforced enum; the vocabulary canary|ci|review-bot|agent|human-audit|user-report is documented as the recommended set (the metrics lens buckets unknown tokens under 'other'), so new channels never require a code change and create never fails on the value.\n\nReducer/schema projection (the CREATE reducer whitelists projected keys, so 'tolerated' is not enough): process_create surfaces detected_by additively and present-only, mirroring the existing source_*/creation_channel projection blocks (src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:112-138), so the field appears in compiled state and 'rebar show' while an event WITHOUT it reduces byte-identically to today. The optional field is declared in the compiled-state schema alongside creation_channel.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/composer.py: create_core reads the env var and accepts an explicit detected_by param (env is the default, explicit wins); create_cli maps the optional --detected-by flag onto that param; _lib_writes/_mcp_writes pass through unchanged (env still applies to them)\n- src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py: process_create copies detected_by into compiled state present-only (mirroring the source_* block)\n- src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json: declare the optional detected_by string field\n- docs: config/env-vars registry entry + agent guidance line\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: env var set -> field present in event, in compiled state, and shown by 'rebar show' — for CLI AND for library create_ticket (proving the seam placement). Flag overrides env. Edge: neither set -> field absent from event AND compiled state byte-identical to pre-change reduction (additivity proof). Validation rows: empty string / whitespace-only -> field absent, create succeeds; mixed-case with padding (' Canary ') -> stamped as 'canary'; unknown token ('fuzzer') -> stamped verbatim, create succeeds. Schema round-trip: compiled state with detected_by validates against ticket_state.schema.json.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] REBAR_DETECTED_BY env var stamps detected_by on created tickets; --detected-by flag overrides; absence changes nothing.\n- [ ] Normalization is strip+lowercase; empty/whitespace-only is treated as unset; unknown tokens are stamped verbatim (no enum enforcement); create never fails on the value.\n- [ ] process_create projects detected_by present-only into compiled state (mirroring source_*), and an event without the field reduces byte-identically to today; ticket_state.schema.json declares the optional field.\n- [ ] Registered in the env-var/docs registry so the drift gate covers it.\n- [ ] Tests cover env, flag, absence, precedence, the validation rows (empty, whitespace, mixed-case+padding, unknown token), the reducer projection + byte-identical-absence property, and the schema round-trip.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine.py","reason":"create path: accept/stamp detected_by field"},{"path":"src/rebar/cli.py","reason":"--detected-by flag + REBAR_DETECTED_BY env"},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"MCP create tool arg"},{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"field documentation"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","e690-1a68-813d-4fc9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"bd354cd2-2066-470f-afd7-9851a6c333af","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bug-trends"],"ticket_id":"d3ed-88e3-86a3-4918","ticket_type":"task","title":"detected-by capture at bug creation (env var for automation, optional flag for agents)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d0be519c-efdd-4e13-8794-79c5865ef434","14481191-c4f1-43f7-a7e3-7cac1f69d09a","52220691-2813-45e1-89c6-5a2738c11094","6aced119-836e-4a7a-937f-a6dc23f0368f","ea7fe70b-35d4-434c-b8dc-4b8a23c7ed89","6d35b6cf-3cde-489f-9dde-68f89ab6ce5b","bd354cd2-2066-470f-afd7-9851a6c333af","5c972665-b4b8-469d-a2